1
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:22,000
Purgatory is a fantasy, western, tv movie film directed by Uli Edel.

2
00:12:32,000 --> 00:12:38,000
An outlaw band flees a posse and rides into Refuge, a small town
where no one carries a gun, drinks, or swears.

3
00:18:48,000 --> 00:18:54,000
The town is actually Purgatory, and the peaceful inhabitants are all famous dead outlaws and criminals such as
Doc Holiday and Wild Bill Hickok who must redeem themselves before gaining admittance to Heaven...

4
00:25:04,000 --> 00:25:10,000
or screw up and go to Hell.

5
00:31:20,000 --> 00:31:26,000
Sheriff Forrest / Wild Bill Hickock, played by Sam Shepard.

6
00:37:36,000 --> 00:37:42,000
Blackjack Britton, played by Eric Roberts.

7
00:43:52,000 --> 00:43:58,000
Doc Woods / Doc Holliday, played by Randy Quaid.

8
00:50:08,000 --> 00:50:14,000
Cavin Guthrie, played by Peter Stormare.

9
00:56:24,000 --> 00:56:30,000
Leon 'Sonny' Miller, played by Brad Rowe.

10
01:02:40,000 --> 01:02:46,000
Deputy Glen / Billy the Kid, played by Donnie Wahlberg.

11
01:08:56,000 --> 01:09:02,000
Purgatory, also known as Purgatory West of the Pecos, is a 1999 American
Western fantasy television film directed by Uli Edel.

12
01:15:12,000 --> 01:15:18,000
The film premiered on TNT on January 10, 1999.

13
01:21:28,000 --> 01:21:34,000
It focuses on a gang of outlaws who find their way to a hidden valley and a peaceful town, where residents
shun swearing, alcohol, guns, and any kind of violence, but resemble dead Western heroes.

14
01:27:44,000 --> 01:27:50,000
The outcome is marked by its exploration of the interface
between legend-making and humanitarian values.
